          "articles": []
        },
        {
          "handle": "MarioNawfal",
          "creator": "@MarioNawfal",
          "text": "🇩🇪 🇺🇦 🇱🇹 A secret antenna found near Leipzig/Halle Airport was used to guide an explosive drone toward Ukrainian cargo planes. German investigators say the antenna boosted control signals during the suspected sabotage attempt on August 4. The drone had been specially modified with an extra battery, camera, 5G router and dual SIM cards. It flew dark, no navigation lights, and was steered over the cellular network, raising the possibility it was operated from another country entirely. DNA recovered from both the drone and 600 grams of unexploded Semtex has pointed investigators toward Lithuania.",
          "link": "https://nitter.net/MarioNawfal/status/2087207415666073943#m",
          "date_utc": "2026-08-11T16:00:00+00:00",
          "is_curated": false,
