        {
          "handle": "MarioNawfal",
          "creator": "@MarioNawfal",
          "text": "🇹🇷🇮🇱 Pravin Sawhney argues that a direct Turkey-Israel conflict could expose a fundamental weakness in NATO: collective defense may not mean much if Washington refuses to act. He says Erdogan understands that West Asia is changing, while China and Russia are pushing a different model based on negotiation, sovereignty and “collective security.” And then comes the provocative part: “America... will not participate in a NATO attack to support Turkey against Israel.” Hypothetical, he stresses. But the implications are enormous. @PravinSawhney Video Mario Nawfal (@MarioNawfal) 🇨🇳🇷🇺 Pravin Sawhney: ",
          "link": "https://nitter.net/MarioNawfal/status/2087203558492197179#m",
          "date_utc": "2026-08-11T15:44:41+00:00",
          "is_curated": false,
