        {
          "handle": "MarioNawfal",
          "creator": "@MarioNawfal",
          "text": "🇮🇱🇹🇷 Israel and Turkey both keep troops on foreign soil while trading accusations. Turkey’s moves draw on a neoOttoman vision that blends Islamic leadership claims with control over former imperial lands, justifying bases in Syria, Iraq and Cyprus as both security buffers and a return to regional centrality. Israel’s expansions lean on biblical Greater Israel language from the Nile to the Euphrates in its maximal form that far right coalition voices treat as divine entitlement, turning post2023 buffer zones in Syria, Lebanon and Gaza into facts on the ground. One side invokes the caliphate’s s",
          "link": "https://nitter.net/MarioNawfal/status/2087202882890432664#m",
